@@ -159,6 +159,18 @@ Given an Exp 3882 seed evaluation, the artifact sets `positive_control_passed`,
 ## SCENARIO-EBT-3882-ADJUDICATION: Beam Accuracy Decides The Kill-Gate
 Given positive-control AR accuracy in `[0.4, 0.95]`, Exp 3882 writes ARTIFACT when beam accuracy is at least half the AR accuracy, writes FUNDAMENTAL when both beam and greedy argmin are below 20% of AR accuracy, and writes INCONCLUSIVE otherwise. Given failed AR headroom, it writes `complete: thesis_a_partb_INCONCLUSIVE_no_headroom_ar<best>` and does not label the result ARTIFACT or FUNDAMENTAL.
 
+## REQ-EBT-3883: Thesis-A System-2 K-Curve On Confirmed-Headroom Checkpoint
+The system must provide `scripts/experiments/experiment_3883_ebt_system2_kcurve.py` to isolate the EBT System-2 K-scaling claim on the same confirmed-headroom checkpoint selected by Exp 3882. The workflow must check CUDA before live work, import `thesis_a_part_b_scaled` by inserting the repository `scripts/` directory on `sys.path`, read `results/experiment_3882_thesis_a_partb_killgate.json`, require `positive_control_passed=true`, load the selected seed checkpoint, and otherwise write a terminal `blocked_upstream_no_headroom` artifact without fabricating a curve. For K in `[1, 2, 4, 8, 16]`, the workflow must decode the held-out split with K-step EBT energy descent from the fixed checkpoint, record held-out accuracy, classify the curve as `MONOTONE_GAIN`, `PLATEAU`, or `DEGRADING`, and write `results/experiment_3883_ebt_system2_kcurve.json` with bare JSON values for `accuracy_by_k`, `k_curve_shape`, `best_k`, `best_k_accuracy`, `n_heldout`, `seeds_used`, `preconditions_checked`, `model_specs`, `random_seed`, `reproducibility_checksum`, `duration_s`, and `inference_substrate`.
+
+## SCENARIO-EBT-3883-UPSTREAM: Missing Headroom Blocks K-Curve Claims
+Given the Exp 3882 artifact is missing, does not set `positive_control_passed=true`, lacks a selected-seed checkpoint, or the checkpoint cannot be loaded, Exp 3883 writes `honest_verdict="blocked_upstream_no_headroom"`, leaves the K-curve metrics empty or null, records the failed precondition evidence, and does not call the System-2 claim supported or bounded.
+
+## SCENARIO-EBT-3883-SCHEMA: K-Curve Artifact Fields Are Bare Values
+Given an Exp 3883 K sweep completes, the artifact sets `accuracy_by_k`, `k_curve_shape`, `best_k`, `best_k_accuracy`, `n_heldout`, `seeds_used`, `preconditions_checked`, `model_specs`, `random_seed`, `reproducibility_checksum`, `duration_s`, and `inference_substrate` as bare JSON bools, numbers, strings, arrays, or objects. None of those fields may be wrapped in a `{value, principle}` dictionary.
+
+## SCENARIO-EBT-3883-FALSIFICATION: Monotone K Gain Is Required For System-2 Support
+Given `accuracy_by_k` for K values `[1, 2, 4, 8, 16]`, Exp 3883 writes `k_curve_shape="MONOTONE_GAIN"` only when the curve is non-decreasing and K=16 accuracy is greater than K=1 accuracy; this yields a `complete: ebt_system2_SUPPORTED_acc_rises_with_k_best_k<k>_acc<a>` verdict. If the curve plateaus or degrades, Exp 3883 writes `complete: ebt_system2_BOUNDED_<shape>_no_usable_descent_signal_at_scale`.
+
 ## REQ-EBT-3731: Thesis-A EBT Bring-Up Capstone Aggregation
 The system must provide `scripts/experiment_3731_capstone_v341.py` to aggregate Exp 3724 through Exp 3730 from checked-in JSON artifacts only. The capstone must exclude any upstream artifact carrying `flagged_adversarial=true` from headline aggregation, cite every unflagged upstream artifact with imported fields and SHA256 hashes, preserve the paper-ready and frozen-headline invariants from Exp 3724, carry the kill-gate part-(a) verdict from Exp 3729, and write `results/experiment_3731_capstone_v341.json` with the required principle-annotated fields. The capstone must not claim that energy-as-generator works; `green_light_342=true` only means stable enough to run the matched-compute comparison, while `green_light_342=false` records Thesis-A as bounded at small scale.
 
